notes.body:
@alagoutte 

Yes, I used the same display filter intentionally for all the PeerNode/PeerAdj/PeerSet SID TLVs, here. Is it OK from the perspective of the wireshark design guideline?

I can use different ones like "peer_node.sid", "peer_adj.sid", or "peer_set.sid", but I would like to keep using the same display filters for each attribute (flags/weight/label/index) in Peer SID TLVs. It might be too much to define each display filter per attribute per Peer SID TLV.

